  "details": "The Problem:\n\nRight now, when you play VRChat on a desktop or phone, trying to click menus, draw, or play mini-games is annoying. To point at anything, you have to move your camera, which makes your whole screen and avatar spin around.\n\nThe Idea:\n\nSince VRChat just added a way for desktop users to move their avatar's arms with the mouse, we should use this for a new \"Free-Aim\" button. If you hold down a button, you could just move your pointer around the screen like a regular computer mouse, without moving your camera or spinning your body.\n\nWhy it’s a great fix:\n\n- Easier to use: It makes clicking things, drawing, and playing games much easier and less motion sickness for players with average computers.\n\n- Backwards Compatible: It automatically works with older worlds. Creators won't have to go back and update their worlds for this to work.\n\n- Toggle vs Hold: Since most players are new to VRC, its better to have Hold for default and an optional for Toggle for veteran players",
